# A TEMPLATE. Copy it, don't edit it:  cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# This file is committed to a public repository. Nothing real goes in it — a
# value pasted here is published the moment it is pushed, and stays in the
# history even after it is removed. Put real values in .env.local (gitignored),
# or in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, which overrides both.

# ── Supabase ── app.supabase.com → Project Settings → API ────────────────────

# Public by design: both are compiled into the browser bundle. RLS is what
# protects the data, not the secrecy of this key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Optional, and never NEXT_PUBLIC_: it bypasses RLS entirely.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_role_key_here

# ── Build orchestrator ── the n8n workflow behind the chat, see n8n/README.md ─

# The published workflow's production webhook (/webhook/, not /webhook-test/).
# Without it the chat answers "Building is not connected yet".
# N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=https://<your-instance>.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/api/v1/build

# Sent as the X-QuickStark-Token header, and checked by the Header Auth
# credential on the Webhook node — the same string has to be in both. Not
# optional: the workflow writes to `projects` with the service_role key, so an
# unauthenticated webhook lets anyone who learns the URL overwrite any row.
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# N8N_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# ── Stub builder ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to "true" to switch on /api/builder/*, which answers the orchestrator's
# four provisioning calls without building anything, so the chat → build →
# preview → billing loop can be watched working before the real service exists.
# Every reply it gives is marked stub: true and its preview page says so.
# Remove it once there is a real provisioning service, and the build branches
# fail honestly again. See src/app/api/builder/[...step]/route.ts.
# BUILDER_STUB_ENABLED=true

# Verify the whole chain with:  npm run check:builder
